# Social Block domains.
#
# Service headers are machine-readable:  ## <id> | <Category> | <Name>
# The panel uses them to build per-service toggles. Toggle a service off to
# ALLOW it (for example Slack or Discord at work) without turning the whole
# block off.
#
# Edit with:  sudoedit /etc/social-block/domains
# Then re-run: bash install-helper.sh --update-domains
# (that also regenerates the per-service sudo/doas rules).
#
# Hosts entries are exact; add the subdomains you actually use. There are no
# wildcards. The CDN/gateway entries are deliberate: blocking only the landing
# page still lets an already-open tab or desktop app fetch media and reconnect.

